@startuml
!theme materia

<style>
document {
  BackgroundColor transparent
  `materia wants Verdana, which isn't installed
  FontName sans-serif
}
</style>

title
  =Sending data with an API Key
  ==Stroom-Proxy holds no user accounts, so it asks its downstream
end title

participant "Sending system" as client
participant "Stroom-Proxy" as proxy
participant "Stroom\n(downstream)" as stroom

== A key Stroom-Proxy has not seen before ==

client -> proxy: POST /datafeed\nAuthorization: Bearer sak_...
proxy -> proxy: Recognise the API key format,\nlook in the verified key cache
proxy -> stroom: POST /api/apikey/v2/verifyApiKey\nthe key, and the permission it must hold\n//authenticated with the proxy's own credential//
stroom -> stroom: Hash and look up the key,\ncheck it has not expired and that\nits owner holds the permission
stroom --> proxy: 200 with the owner's identity,\nor 404 if the key is not valid
proxy -> proxy: Remember a valid key in memory,\nand write it, hashed, to a local file
proxy --> client: 200

== The same key again ==

client -> proxy: POST /datafeed\nAuthorization: Bearer sak_...
proxy -> proxy: Cache hit, no downstream call
proxy --> client: 200
note right of proxy
  The file is only consulted when
  the downstream cannot be reached.
  It survives a restart, so an outage
  does not stop keys already seen
end note

@enduml
